pi.github.com/users/voylin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-21T04:35:32Z","updated_at":"2026-02-21T04:35:32Z","body":"Made a rebase to fix the merge conflicts which were because of \"automatically opening scripts\" being merged before this one. There was a slight issue with resolving which caused the check to fail, fixed it so all should be good again now. Please let me know if something else needs to be done, I need this fix to improve my workflow in the editor.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3938149935/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3938447742","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115554#issuecomment-3938447742","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115554","id":3938447742,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7qv_F-","user":{"login":"voylin","id":56970759,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2OTcwNzU5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56970759?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin","html_url":"https://github.com/voylin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-21T08:27:09Z","updated_at":"2026-02-21T08:27:09Z","body":"> I want to propose making the option to use fuzzy search or not a toggle / dropdown next to the search field. In CLion, I often use both \"case sensitive\" search and \"case insensitive\" search, depending on the situation, and having a toggle available right when I search is extremely useful. I can imagine us adding options for case sensitivity and regex search also, in the future.\r\n\r\nAdding a toggle on the right of the file dock search would be possible for the layout without making the area too busy looking.\r\n<img width=\"303\" height=\"112\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/397b0315-f0de-4118-91d4-d1836f358682\" />\r\n\r\nBut for the scene tree dock I think this would cause problems as there's already a lot of buttons around it, I guess this will make it a bit too overwhelming there.\r\n<img width=\"310\" height=\"88\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9a3573c7-10f3-4350-bee3-22910f6d65c5\" />\r\n\r\nWhat do you think?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3938447742/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3973184065","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115554#issuecomment-3973184065","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115554","id":3973184065,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7s0fpB","user":{"login":"AdriaandeJongh","id":5611323,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MTEzMjM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5611323?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh","html_url":"https://github.com/AdriaandeJongh","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-27T14:15:22Z","updated_at":"2026-02-27T14:15:22Z","body":"I agree that more buttons next to the search field will make it very crowded. I'm inclined to say that wanting to add more buttons / functionality around the search fields will require another proposal, perhaps one that makes the search icon on the right a dropdown with settings, but that would put it outside of the scope of this PR.\r\n\r\nI still agree with my earlier comment that alongside the other fuzzy matching option at `filesystem/quick_open_dialog/enable_fuzzy_matching`, we should give the two new settings proposed here the same names and the same options, including the 'fuzzy misses'. If we can do that, then I'd approve this from a usability perspective at least.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3973184065/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3975872481","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115554#issuecomment-3975872481","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115554","id":3975872481,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7s-v_h","user":{"login":"voylin","id":56970759,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2OTcwNzU5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56970759?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin","html_url":"https://github.com/voylin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-28T00:35:50Z","updated_at":"2026-02-28T00:35:50Z","body":"I'll see what I can do, having a busy week so it might take me a few days to implement this ;)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3975872481/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4069059517","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115554#issuecomment-4069059517","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115554","id":4069059517,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7yiOu9","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-16T16:41:08Z","updated_at":"2026-03-16T16:41:08Z","body":"> the same options, including the 'fuzzy misses'\r\n\r\nI don't think each dock needs its own \"fuzzy misses\" setting. Maybe we could have one global config for fuzzy matching, i.e. a new `editors/fuzzy_matching/` category, which would have toggle for every instance where it can be enabled (e.g. `editors/fuzzy_matching/enable_in_quick_open_dialog`, or with subsections: `editors/fuzzy_matching/enable_for/quick_open_dialog` or similar), and some settings.\r\n\r\nAs for where to put the toggle, in Scene dock it can be in the `⋮` menu, in FileSystem dock you can replace sort menu with `⋮` I guess.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4069059517/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4072567340","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115554#issuecomment-4072567340","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115554","id":4072567340,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7yvnIs","user":{"login":"voylin","id":56970759,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2OTcwNzU5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56970759?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin","html_url":"https://github.com/voylin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-17T05:58:53Z","updated_at":"2026-03-17T05:58:53Z","body":"> I don't think each dock needs its own \"fuzzy misses\" setting. Maybe we could have one global config for fuzzy matching, i.e. a new `editors/fuzzy_matching/` category, which would have toggle for every instance where it can be enabled (e.g. `editors/fuzzy_matching/enable_in_quick_open_dialog`, or with subsections: `editors/fuzzy_matching/enable_for/quick_open_dialog` or similar), and some settings.\r\n\r\nI've added the fuzzy matching setting category and for now I've made it like this: `editors/fuzzy_matching/enable_for/quick_open_dialog`. Also added the _rename_settings for compatibility but not certain if this is entirely needed.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"886\" height=\"233\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ae40d1aa-4e14-4f30-bde8-071b61741ff9\" />\r\n\r\nAlso changed to use the fuzzy search class but I'm not 100% certain if I implemented it correctly so I'd like someone to check it please. ^^\" I mean ... it works, but it's not because it works that it's the correct way of using implementing it and I just want to be certain.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"294\" height=\"183\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/06dc743a-9a8b-467f-8e2a-623c2ce80b4e\" />","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4072567340/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4080797215","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115554#issuecomment-4080797215","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115554","id":4080797215,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7zPAYf","user":{"login":"AdriaandeJongh","id":5611323,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MTEzMjM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5611323?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh","html_url":"https://github.com/AdriaandeJongh","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-18T08:52:56Z","updated_at":"2026-03-18T08:52:56Z","body":"Consolidating the settings to one place is a good call!\r\n\r\nTested this and found that filtering based on 1 or 2 characters no longer works.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4080797215/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4080815439","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115554#issuecomment-4080815439","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115554","id":4080815439,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7zPE1P","user":{"login":"voylin","id":56970759,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2OTcwNzU5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56970759?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin","html_url":"https://github.com/voylin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-18T08:56:16Z","updated_at":"2026-03-18T08:56:16Z","body":"> Consolidating the settings to one place is a good call!\r\n> \r\n> Tested this and found that filtering based on 1 or 2 characters no longer works.\r\n\r\nIn what way did it no longer work exactly? Is it possible that the `max misses` is messing with the expected results? ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4080815439/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4080872696","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115554#issuecomment-4080872696","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115554","id":4080872696,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7zPSz4","user":{"login":"AdriaandeJongh","id":5611323,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MTEzMjM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5611323?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh","html_url":"https://github.com/AdriaandeJongh","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-18T09:06:02Z","updated_at":"2026-03-18T09:06:02Z","body":"Hmm. With the current design, inherent to `editors/fuzzy_matching/max_fuzzy_misses` is that it also defines how many characters you **have** to enter before filtering will start working at all... But that is a bit of a step back in the functionality of filtering with characters fewer than the misses + 1.\r\n\r\nFor example:\r\n<img width=\"278\" height=\"183\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-03-18 at 10 00 22\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ca59af6d-b082-4bdf-8061-fff116043402\" />\r\n\r\nBecause `max_fuzzy_misses` is 2, filtering won't work at all.\r\n\r\nI wonder if there should be different rules for the amount of character that are less or equal to `max_fuzzy_misses`.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4080872696/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4080893928","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115554#issuecomment-4080893928","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115554","id":4080893928,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7zPX_o","user":{"login":"voylin","id":56970759,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2OTcwNzU5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56970759?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin","html_url":"https://github.com/voylin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"pub